            <h2>Page 1</h2>
            <h1>Truths vs Myths</h1>
            <h4>Problematic social media use occurs when screen time turns into a repetitive habit that disrupts a persons physical and mental health. This is driven by platform algorithms engineered around variable reward loops, similar to slot machines. By tracking your data these systems give an addictive feed designed to trigger dopamine hits and keep you scrolling endlessly.</h4>
        </div>
        <div>
            <img class="small" src="static/truthvsmyth.jpg" alt="Image of Truths VS Myths">
            <h4>However the idea that social media is entirely harmful is a myth. Research proves it is a double edged sword while passive scrolling causes harm, active use can support genuine connection, identity exploration, and mental health support. Ultimately we are not all clinically addicted, but we are heavily conditioned by platforms that feed on our attention spans.</h4>
